<title>USA: Thailand files $1 bln shelf for notes and/or bonds.</title>
<headline>Thailand files $1 bln shelf for notes and/or bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kingdom of Thailand Wednesday filed a shelf registration with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $1 billion in notes and/or bonds and warrants.</p>
<p>When combined with a previous registration, Thailand will have a total $1.45 billion in securities available for sale, the filing said.  </p>
<p>Net proceeds from the sale of the securities will be used to finance various public sector investment projects, the filing said.</p>
